    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0582" n="1416" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1416"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/234</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-20T12:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 20, 1918, 12 noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 20, 8.20 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9130. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 309. Cecil has just
                    informed me that he cabled the British Embassy late last night saying that His
                    Majesty’s Government considered the Dutch had refused proposal which was to
                    expire on the 18th, adding that they were prepared to requisition Dutch boats
                    and asking when you were doing likewise, so that the action might be
                    simultaneous. I take it, therefore, that you will be taking such steps
                    immediately.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
